# Simorgh backend — sample environment configuration
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values for your deployment.

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3001

# ── MongoDB (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
DATABASE_NAME=simorgh_db

# ── SQL Server (EPLAN parts) — optional ───────────────────────────────────
SQL_USER=userfanni
SQL_PASSWORD=12345678
SQL_SERVER=192.168.1.39
SQL_DATABASE=Eplan_n2
SQL_PORT=1433

# ── MySQL (TPMS) — optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# MYSQL_HOST=...
# MYSQL_USER=...
# MYSQL_PASSWORD=...
# MYSQL_DATABASE=...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI CHATBOT — LOCAL (offline) model
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three ways to point the chatbot at a local model, listed in priority order.
# Set ONE of them; the rest can stay commented out.
#
# ─ A) llm-gateway (preferred when running inside simorgh-agent on .68) ─
# Uses the unified gateway that already routes text→.61 and image→.62,
# handles online/offline fallback, strips <think> tags, etc.
#
#   LLM_GATEWAY_URL=http://llm-gateway:8030
#   LLM_GATEWAY_MODE=offline      # offline | online | auto
#
# Outside the docker network, route through host nginx:
#   LLM_GATEWAY_URL=http://192.168.1.68/api/llm-gateway
#
# ─ B) Direct to the Simorgh local LLM cluster (.61) — recommended for the
#      stand-alone simorgh-soft backend ─
# OpenAI-compatible API on :80, model `gpt-oss-20b` (Unsloth+vLLM+FastAPI).
#
#   LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://192.168.1.61/v1/chat/completions
#   LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=gpt-oss-20b
#
# Notes:
#   • The .61 nginx IP-allowlists 192.168.1.68 + localhost. If this backend
#     runs on a different host, either move it to .68 or open the allowlist
#     in `llms/nginx_configs/conf.d/llm.conf` on .61.
#   • For the VLM box use `LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://192.168.1.62/v1/chat/completions`
#     and `LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5-vl-7b`.
#
# ─ C) Any other OpenAI-compatible local server (LM Studio, llama.cpp,
#      personal vLLM, Ollama via openai-compat shim, …) ─
#
#   LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions
#   LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=<whatever the server reports in /v1/models>
#   LOCAL_MODEL_KEY=optional-bearer-token
#
# ─ D) Ollama directly (no OpenAI compat layer) ─
# Detected automatically when the URL ends with /api/chat.
#
#   LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat
#   LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=llama3.1
#
# Defaults (used when no override is set):
#   LOCAL_MODEL_URL  = http://192.168.1.61/v1/chat/completions
#   LOCAL_MODEL_NAME = gpt-oss-20b

# Active config — uncomment to override the defaults above.
# LLM_GATEWAY_URL=http://llm-gateway:8030
# LLM_GATEWAY_MODE=offline
# LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://192.168.1.61/v1/chat/completions
# LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=gpt-oss-20b
# LOCAL_MODEL_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI CHATBOT — ONLINE model (optional)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible API (OpenAI, OpenRouter, Together, Groq, …).
# Same JSON tool-call protocol as the local endpoint.

# ONLINE_MODEL_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# ONLINE_MODEL_KEY=sk-...
# ONLINE_MODEL_NAME=gpt-4o-mini
